I guess expectations in this newsgroup are higher than average. This may
be because NetHack is a game that attracts a different audience than
most games. Without wanting to boast, I think the average reader in this
group is more educated than the average newsgroup reader.

I believe - but have no backup on this - that in the past, more
newsgroups were like this group: more polite, more strict, more
"policed". Norms and standards were stricter then.

This newsgroup managed to maintain those higher standards, while most
other groups slowly but surely went downhill. I think the policing that
takes place here is the most important reason for the maintenance of
quality postings here (few abbrevations, no top posting, trimming of
messages, etc.).

